===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[hasty]] manner; [[quickly]] or [[hurriedly]].
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=5|passage=The departure was not unduly prolonged.{{...}}Within the door Mrs. Spoker '''hastily''' imparted to Mrs. Love a few final sentiments on the subject of Divine Intention in the disposition of buckets; farewells and last commiserations; a deep, guttural instigation to the horse; and the wheels of the waggonette crunched heavily away into obscurity.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1945|month=September and October|author=C. Hamilton Ellis|title=Royal Trains—V|journal=Railway Magazine|page=251|text=The last occasion on which the Kaiser [Wilhelm II] used this train was for an inglorious journey into Holland towards the end of the 1914 war. He spent the night in it at Eysden [{{l|en|Eijsden}}], while the Queen of the Netherlands and a '''hastily''' summoned Cabinet debated what to do with him.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1966|author=James Workman|title=The Mad Emperor|publisher=Scripts|location=Melbourne, Sydney|page=40|passage=Eudemis moved '''hastily''' but as unobtrusively as he could through the gaping crowd[.]}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[soon|Soon]], [[shortly]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|II|vi|passage=she with liquors strong his eyes did steepe, / That nothing should him '''hastily''' awake [...].}}

